# Line endings.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows checks out CRLF. That is harmless for
# most of the tree and fatal for a shell script: `#!/bin/sh` followed by a
# carriage return fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", and the git
# hooks in scripts/hooks/ are shell scripts whose whole job is to survive
# a fresh clone and be reinstalled. They were committed from a Windows
# checkout, which is where this was noticed.
#
# The Enlightened Lifter repo has carried `* text=auto eol=lf` for a while;
# this one had no .gitattributes at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
